\ A generic native whose dispatch lookup misses must release the operands it
\ popped before raising. The operands here are refcounted struct instances and
\ containers, so a missing release shows up as a GPA leak report on stderr,
\ which this test's empty stderr golden rejects.
\
\ Each path is driven repeatedly so one leaked operand per call accumulates,
\ then asserted once for the error itself. The repetition is written inline
\ rather than through a helper word: a word body that passes its own quotation
\ parameter to `times` miscompiles under `--compile=eager`, a known open bug.

use "testing" ;

boxed: struct{ a } ;

"sequence access misses" test-section

20 [ [ 1 make-boxed #len drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
20 [ [ 1 make-boxed 0 #nth drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
20 [ [ V{ 1 2 } >hash drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
[ 1 make-boxed #len drop ] "#len on a struct raises" assert-error
[ 1 make-boxed 0 #nth drop ] "#nth on a struct raises" assert-error
[ V{ 1 2 } >hash drop ] ">hash on a vector raises" assert-error

"bitwise misses" test-section

20 [ [ 1 make-boxed 1 bitand drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
20 [ [ 1 make-boxed 1 bitor drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
20 [ [ 1 make-boxed 1 bitxor drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
20 [ [ 1 make-boxed bitnot drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
20 [ [ 1 make-boxed 1 shift-left drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
20 [ [ 1 make-boxed 1 shift-right drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
20 [ [ 1 make-boxed 1 ushift-right drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
20 [ [ 1 make-boxed 1 shift drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
[ 1 make-boxed 1 bitand drop ] "bitand on a struct raises" assert-error
[ 1 make-boxed bitnot drop ] "bitnot on a struct raises" assert-error
[ 1 make-boxed 1 shift drop ] "shift on a struct raises" assert-error

\ A non-fixnum shift count is rejected before the value is inspected, so the
\ count and the value take separate release paths.
20 [ [ 1 make-boxed V{ 1 } shift-left drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
[ 1 make-boxed V{ 1 } shift-left drop ] "non-fixnum shift count raises" assert-error

"symbol conversion miss" test-section

20 [ [ 1 make-boxed >symbol drop ] [ drop ] recover ] times
[ 1 make-boxed >symbol drop ] ">symbol on a struct raises" assert-error

\ The success arm hands its slice to the pushed symbol rather than releasing it.
"ok" >symbol ok: "string converts to a symbol" assert=
